# Env

Copy to `.env` locally. After merge, Developer sets **secrets** on Railway (`TELNYX_API_KEY`, `XAI_API_KEY`, `API_KEY`). Do not place real PSTN calls from this repo. Tests mock Telnyx and xAI.

## Required for outbound calls

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `TELNYX_API_KEY` | Telnyx Call Control API (Bearer). Set on Railway after merge. |
| `XAI_API_KEY` | xAI Grok Voice Live 2. Set on Railway after merge. |
| `API_KEY` | Bearer token for `POST /api/outbound` and `GET /api/calls/:id`. Set on Railway after merge. |
| `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | Public HTTPS origin. Telnyx webhook = `{PUBLIC_BASE_URL}/webhooks/telnyx`. |

## Telnyx (non-secret, TRNSF/Nuno)

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `TELNYX_CONNECTION_ID` | `3041732714274227469` | Call Control app **TRNSX-Outbound-Grok**. |
| `TELNYX_OUTBOUND_VOICE_PROFILE_ID` | `3041732644774610184` | Outbound Voice Profile bound to that app (not sent on each dial). |
| `FROM_NUMBER` | `+351210210260` | Caller ID. |

## Voice / model

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GROK_VOICE` | `ara` | Grok Voice Live 2 voice. Keep `ara` unless explicitly overridden. |
| `GROK_MODEL` | `grok-voice-think-fast-2.0` | Grok Voice Live 2 model. |
| `GROK_VOICE_SPEED` | `1.05` | Documented xAI `audio.output.speed` (0.7–1.5). Slight liveliness nudge above the API default `1.0`. |

Language on each call: `pt-PT` | `en-GB` | `en-US` (default `pt-PT` if omitted).

Persona (`greeting`) and `objective` come from `POST /api/outbound`. There is no branded spoken default and no recording notice. If `greeting` is omitted, the service composes `Olá`/`Hello` + Lisbon time-of-day + a short natural ask derived from `objective` (never a ROLEPLAY/prompt dump). Optional `spokenAsk` is a clean one-line ask. Optional `timezone` (IANA, default `Europe/Lisbon`) selects the local clock. `waitForCallee` does not require `greeting`.

## Turn-taking (Grok server_vad)

Phone-tuned so the agent answers promptly after the callee stops (default 160ms silence). The Telnyx↔Grok bridge forwards audio immediately (no extra debounce after `speech_stopped`). Override if needed:

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `GROK_VAD_THRESHOLD` | `0.5` | VAD activation (`0.1`–`0.9`). |
| `GROK_VAD_SILENCE_MS` | `160` | End-of-turn silence in ms before the model replies. |
| `GROK_VAD_PREFIX_PADDING_MS` | `200` | Audio kept before detected speech start (barge-in). |
| `GROK_VAD_IDLE_TIMEOUT_MS` | `12000` | Idle timeout (not the turn gap). |
| `GROK_CALLEE_SPEECH_GRACE_MS` | `1000` | After answer/stream start, ignore `speech_started` (ringback/noise) before waitForCallee can unlock via duration. |
| `GROK_CALLEE_MIN_SPEECH_MS` | `130` | Minimum accepted utterance length after grace (waitForCallee). Short greetings («estou», «alô», «sim») and any non-empty transcript unlock immediately. |
| `GROK_HANGUP_PLAYOUT_MS` | `1000` | Extra Telnyx playout after Grok `response.done` before hangup on `end_call`. |

## Optional

| Variable | Purpose |
| --- | --- |
| `RESULT_WEBHOOK` | `POST` JSON when a call ends. Empty disables. |
| `TELNYX_PUBLIC_KEY` | Account Ed25519 public key. When set, `/webhooks/telnyx` verifies signatures. |
| `XAI_BASE_URL` | Default `https://api.x.ai`. |
| `TELNYX_API_BASE` | Default `https://api.telnyx.com`. |
| `PORT` | Railway injects this. Default `3000`. |
| `MAX_CALL_SECONDS` | Hard cap before hangup. Default `600`. |

This service is **outbound-only** and is **not** Alice.
